  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "The sum of two numbers is \\(S.\\) Suppose \\(3\\) is added to each number and then each of the resulting numbers is doubled. What is the sum of the final two numbers?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2S+3\\)",
    "B": "\\(3S+2\\)",
    "C": "\\(3S+6\\)",
    "D": "\\(2S+6\\)",
    "E": "\\(2S+12\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "We can follow the sum without knowing the individual numbers. Adding \\(3\\) to each of two numbers adds \\(3+3=6\\) to their sum, making it \\(S+6\\). Doubling each resulting number doubles their sum, so the final sum is\n\\[\n2(S+6)=2S+12.\n\\]\nThus the answer is \\(\\boxed{2S+12}\\), choice E.",
